The mirror of the $\mathrm{C}^1$ line above: a maximum over the $0$-inputs
is a maximum over a subset of the domain. Recorded at <code>partial</code> rather
than <code>relation</code> only because $\mathrm{C}^0$ needs a distinguished &quot;no&quot;
answer to mean anything, so the relational cell is not the zoo's to fill;
the bound still travels up to <code>total</code> on its own.

